.TH ac 1 "FUZIX System Utilities" "FUZIX"
.SH NAME
ac \- how long people have been logged in
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ac
[\fB\-w\fI wtmp\fR] [\fB\-d\fR] [\fB\-p\fR] [\fIuser\fR ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ac
adds up the connect time recorded in
.B /var/run/wtmp
and prints the total in hours.  With
.IR user s
named, only those are counted.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-w " wtmp"
Read a different file.
.TP
.B \-d
Print a line for each day.
.TP
.B \-p
Print a line for each person.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /var/run/wtmp
.SH NOTES
On a single-user machine this is a curiosity rather than an accounting
tool, but it does answer how many hours the thing has actually been used
for.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR who (1),
.BR uptime (1),
.BR accton (1)
